<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds ended off highs on a wave of late profit taking, seen also on the other peripheral markets, dealers said.</p>
<p>But the mood remains positive even after recent big gains, they said, adding that they expect further gains ahead of Spain's 1997 budget, due before month-end.</p>
<p>Ten-year September bond futures, traded for the last time today, hit a high of 104.06.</p>
<p>The December contract ended at 103.25, with roll-over operations keeping dealers busy in the afternoon.</p>
</text>
